  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;be a differentiable function in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
